body:
Exposes the Copilot SDK's [`SystemMessageConfig`](https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/copilot-sdk/getting-started#customize-the-system-message) in `AgentSpec`, allowing callers to control the system prompt via append, replace, or customize modes.

## Changes

- **`AgentSpec`** — adds optional `systemMessage?: SystemMessageConfig` field (type imported directly from `@github/copilot-sdk`)
- **`normalizeSpec`** — propagates `systemMessage` through spec normalization
- **`resolveCallRuntime`** — includes `systemMessage` in the resolved runtime
- **`createCopilotSession`** — accepts and forwards `systemMessage` to `client.createSession`

## Example

```ts
// Append mode (default): extra instructions appended to SDK-managed prompt
agent({ name: "assistant", systemMessage: { content: "Always be concise." } });

// Customize mode: section-level overrides
agent({
  name: "assistant",
  systemMessage: {
    mode: "customize",
    sections: {
      tone: { action: "replace", content: "Warm and professional." },
      code_change_rules: { action: "remove" },
    },
  },
});

// Replace mode: full control, bypasses SDK guardrails
agent({ name: "assistant", systemMessage: { mode: "replace", content: "You are..." } });
```
